; triggers-schedules: pulse is a one-beat grid phased to start at beat 1 and
; targets a four-lane bus, so its write is (phase, count, gate, beats-since).
; hit is an explicit ascending list into a scalar target, so only phase fits.
; Before the first event a trigger writes nothing; the loop resets both.
(transport :bpm 120 :meter [4 4] :dur 2bar :end loop)

(trigger :target pulse :every 1b :offset 1b)
(trigger :target hit :at [2b 5b 7b])
